ichaelChaban","id":76599514,"login":"MichaelChaban","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NTk5NTE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/commits/2f164906299f1289d75a34f19397c6eb5434187c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:46:41Z","email":"cmisa695@gmail.com","name":"Michael Chaban"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:46:41Z","email":"cmisa695@gmail.com","name":"Michael Chaban"},"message":"fix(refunds): a retried card refund asks Stripe for the refund made on its key before sending it again, and a refund Stripe failed is raised to administrators at once [D1]\n\nStripe forgets an idempotency key after about a day and would then pay a late retry as a second refund. Every refund is now tagged at Stripe with RefundKey metadata, and every retry of an existing row (the hourly re-drive, a reused Pending/Failed row, the unique-violation winner) first lists the refunds of the PaymentIntent: a live match is recorded with its Stripe id and the amount Stripe paid, a failed or canceled match closes the row Failed and sends nothing, no match sends on the same key, and a lookup that cannot reach Stripe sends nothing. The hourly job raises refund_needs_retry at once for a row closed because Stripe failed it. The conservation property test now lets Stripe forget its keys and asserts no key is paid twice.","tree":{"sha":"9a641682f5d36ece6553766084732505922596fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/git/trees/9a641682f5d36ece6553766084732505922596fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/git/commits/2f164906299f1289d75a34f19397c6eb5434187c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76599514?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MichaelChaban","id":76599514,"login":"MichaelChaban","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NTk5NTE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/commit/2f164906299f1289d75a34f19397c6eb5434187c","node_id":"C_kwDOPNcZQNoAKDJmMTY0OTA2Mjk5ZjEyODlkNzVhMzRmMTkzOTdjNmViNTQzNDE4N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/commit/bda774b43120ea9fc3c1356dcaead981bf32ee70","sha":"bda774b43120ea9fc3c1356dcaead981bf32ee70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/commits/bda774b43120ea9fc3c1356dcaead981bf32ee70"}],"sha":"2f164906299f1289d75a34f19397c6eb5434187c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/commits/2f164906299f1289d75a34f19397c6eb5434187c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76599514?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChab