arred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/commits/391d5d846a789e7a18781d18301b0344f3d847a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T02:24:25Z","email":"cmisa695@gmail.com","name":"Michael Chaban"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T02:24:25Z","email":"cmisa695@gmail.com","name":"Michael Chaban"},"message":"fix(orders): recording cash on a door default closes the debt''s open pay link first, and a pay link paid after the cash was recorded is refunded\n\nAdminRecordCashReceived wrote the UnpaidCash debt off as paid in cash but left its Stripe Checkout Session payable for up to a day, and the webhook then marked the written-off debt Paid and kept the card payment, so the customer paid the price twice. The handler now expires the session before writing the debt off, refuses with order.payment_not_outstanding when Stripe reports it already paid, and with order.payment_gateway_unavailable when Stripe cannot be reached. As a backstop, SettleReceivable refunds in full a payment of a door price whose order was settled in cash, as it already did for a second payment of a paid debt. The call closes a link and charges nothing, so it is exempt from the card-payments switch, and the admin error contract lists the gateway key.\n\nAlso pins mutation 13: paying the door debt through the pay link webhook grants no loyalty points and leaves the referral Accepted.","tree":{"sha":"60415e2721c312a922ea566fcf9f0511c480fc7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/git/trees/60415e2721c312a922ea566fcf9f0511c480fc7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/git/commits/391d5d846a789e7a18781d18301b0344f3d847a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}}