 customer who owes an amount is refused every booking with a way to pay it, is told when a door price goes unpaid, and reads the cash cap as upcoming bookings [B1, B2, B3]\n\nOwner ruling 2026-10-06. order.unpaid_receivable replaces the retired order.cash_unpaid_receivable in five locales. When the server refuses a booking for it, cash or card, the booking sheet, the schedule form (create and edit) and the recurring confirm open a system dialog with Pay now, which goes to Payments; any other refusal still snackbars. The key is found among every refusal the body carries, split where whole-booking rules share one code. For that the order and schedule repositories now keep the body''s keys on a 400; on the confirm this also brings the terms re-ask after consent.terms_not_accepted to life, which the view model already handled but never received. The order.cash_not_paid push renders under order updates with the order number and the amount owed and opens Payments; it stays out of the feed keyset until the server lists it. The cap-of-2 refusal now says it counts upcoming cash bookings not yet paid, and the Payments intro no longer says card bookings are unaffected.","tree":{"sha":"42b9a112b5a0db501243845656961e18289114e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/git/trees/42b9a112b5a0db501243845656961e18289114e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/git/commits/c2e147cf4a97ff9310c0b1b835d686611870ea66","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76599514?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/