ic"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/commits/f5d2b0351748da0bdc93ac9713382b0422ce1469/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:19:22Z","email":"cmisa695@gmail.com","name":"Michael Chaban"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:19:22Z","email":"cmisa695@gmail.com","name":"Michael Chaban"},"message":"fix(cancellations): a free, admin or no-show cancellation of a partly refunded card order refunds the rest of the sale to the card and the balance, as the terms promise, and records what it gave back [M3]\n\nThe card refund was gated on Paid, so a partly refunded order got back only credit and the card kept the rest. The gate now admits PartiallyRefunded on a fee-free cancellation, the platform cancellation and the no-show, and the seam holds the price asked for to what the sale has left on each tender. A pending refund''s credit leg is no longer followed by a second order-ended-unpaid return. CancellationRefundAmount on a fee-free cancellation is what this cancellation gives back, not the full price again. A no-show announces a pending refund only when its own refund row is pending. Fee-bearing cancellations of partly refunded orders are unchanged and pinned by a characterisation test until the owner rules.","tree":{"sha":"fa3ee199bc450770e86e60394f77f523f5800fa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/git/trees/fa3ee199bc450770e86e60394f77f523f5800fa9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/git/commits/f5d2b0351748da0bdc93ac9713382b0422ce1469","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76599514?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"