.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/commits/f7e3e36e82d5668c57b55b2ca572e60976ae43be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:10:56Z","email":"cmisa695@gmail.com","name":"Michael Chaban"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:10:56Z","email":"cmisa695@gmail.com","name":"Michael Chaban"},"message":"fix(refunds): a card refund left pending, which Stripe may already have paid, counts against every other refund, complaint settled in credit and credit return on its order, and its retry keeps its card amount [M2]\n\nA pending row now counts wherever a ceiling or what-is-left is computed, except the row being retried. A retried row keeps the amount it froze, so Stripe sees the same amount on the same key and replays the refund it made; a complaint settled in credit since then comes off the row''s credit leg instead. The order-ended-unpaid credit return ignores a pending card refund on an order that never took payment [X3]. The money-conservation property test now lets any refund be paid and unrecorded at any step, settles complaints through the production ResolveDispute handler, and fails on over-return.","tree":{"sha":"76630f35f2c3cdbabcabb64f0e620037e0b6dbc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/git/trees/76630f35f2c3cdbabcabb64f0e620037e0b6dbc4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/git/commits/f7e3e36e82d5668c57b55b2ca572e60976ae43be","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76599514?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/following