":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:33:50Z","email":"cmisa695@gmail.com","name":"Michael Chaban"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:33:50Z","email":"cmisa695@gmail.com","name":"Michael Chaban"},"message":"docs: iOS''s schedules list hides Create from a paused Plus member and says why, as Android does [Z-1]\n\nDocuments 911dafc33. business-rules.md said iOS still offered a past-due\nor paused member the create button and had no benefits-paused notice,\nand that RecurringListAffordances.of took benefitsPaused. Since Z-1\nneither is true: the gate takes benefitsPaused and has Android''s paused\ncase.\n\n- product/business-rules.md (#deactivated-catalogue): the iOS bullet now\n  describes Android''s table on iOS: Create and Edit only when allowed,\n  the upsell and lapsed notice only for a non-member, and the\n  benefits-paused notice (Android''s copy, five languages) above the cards\n  or in place of the empty state, with no subscribe action. It keeps the\n  slow-read behaviour and pause/resume/delete. The one remaining\n  difference is reported and not changed: iOS''s order detail still\n  offers \"Make this recurring\" to such a member, because\n  OrderDetailViewModel resolves the gate without benefitsPaused. The\n  membership section says both apps refuse authoring with the notice.\n- CHANGELOG: the iOS Changed entry now covers the hidden create button\n  and the notice.","tree":{"sha":"54bd37f4a185ec12d332075a6c686ab3fe9bc1b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/git/trees/54bd37f4a185ec12d332075a6c686ab3fe9bc1b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VM-s-Solutions/cleansia/git/commits/c69dbf5d43f42bfc6eb057852a2548f1f4e1b008","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76599514?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelChaban/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Micha